ions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T17:40:48-07:00","id":1385330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1385308-are-there-going-to-be-any-additional-books-for-wraith-20th?p=1385327#post1385327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, C20 has been getting around that by means of Storyteller's Vault: freelancers who participated in the making of C20 have been publishing unofficial C20 supplements that amount to what they wanted to publish officially.<br /> <br /> So yeah; while it's unlikely that we'll see any more official Wr20 supplements, it's still not entirely outside the realm of possibility that we might end up with some \u201cunofficially official\u201d ones. But only if there's someone who the fans would accept as a valid source for \u201cofficial\u201d material <i>and</i> who is willing and able to take on the extra work needed to publish a STV product.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I probably should have added that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Yeah, stuff from the CtD20 Developers and Freelancers is under the Radio Free Arcadia label. Theres also some nice stuff on there from the Walking Away From Arcadia podcast crew and some independant writers.<br /> <br /> The English translation for Necropolis Venezia is a massive tome of awesome, its still in need of a little editing but the contents are first rate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T08:39:14-07:00","id":1386414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1385308-are-there-going-to-be-any-additional-books-for-wraith-20th?p=1385330#post1385330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The English translation for Necropolis Venezia is a massive tome of awesome, its still in need of a little editing but the contents are first rate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Necropolis Venice? I will have to look that up - a solid wraith book about the city nominally run by the Giovanni sounds interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avata